  "notes": "New catalogs created: photo_catalog.json (entire PHOTO department) and aa_catalog.json (AA 1, the College of Arts and Architecture first-year seminar). Entrance to Major requires PHOTO 200 or PHOTO 202 or a portfolio review -- satisfied directly since PHOTO 202 is an explicit Semester 1 item. Reused ART 122Y/ART 211Y/AED 211W (all already cataloged from Art History, Art Education, and Digital Multimedia Design builds) for the Semester 4 pool item. 2026-08-27 re-verification against the live bulletin's own Suggested Academic Plan tab HTML (DOM-extracted directly, not the summarized page -- a separate sova.psu.edu handbook page failed to load and could not be checked, so this is bulletin-only): found and fixed 3 real bugs. (1) GQ under-wiring: the real Year 1 Spring row has a second General Education Course (GQ) item; only Semester 1 had gen_ed:GQ wired. (2) Semester 3 (Year 2 Fall) had 2 generic Supporting Course items and only 2 plain GEN ED slots, but the real row has 3 plain Gen Ed cells and only 1 Supporting Course cell -- converted the extra Supporting Course back to a plain GEN ED. (3) The bulletin's own footnote 1 names a real, closed 29-course list for Additional Course for Major (18cr total) -- wired all 5 modeled occurrences to it (added COMM/DART/GD/ARCH/INART/LARCH/THEA/MUSIC to departments, needed both for this list and for footnote 2's Supporting Course department list below), excluding ART 122Y/ART 211Y (already the required Semester 4 literal alternative) and PHOTO 404/PHOTO 495 (already separate required Semester 6/8 courses) to avoid the same recommend-the-same-course-forever deadlock found in the Digital Arts and Media Design build; AA 300/400-level (a level range, not an enumerable code) and FRNAR 100 (no FRNAR department catalog exists anywhere in this app; could not be confirmed to exist) were dropped from the list rather than guessed at. Converted one Semester 8 Elective slot into a 6th Additional-Course occurrence to help close the gap between the row grid's own 15cr (5 x 3cr) and the footnote's stated 18cr. Footnote 2's Supporting Course requirement (any of 13 named departments, in consultation with an adviser) is real and genuinely open -- wired all 5 modeled occurrences to open_elective, restricted to that department list by excluding everything else this plan loads (PHOTO itself, ENGL, ESL); the row grid itself only contains 5 Supporting Course cells (15cr) versus the footnote's stated 18cr, a residual minor source-internal reconciliation gap (same kind documented elsewhere this session, e.g. Art History) left undisturbed rather than force-padded with an invented 6th cell the source itself never prints.",
